                    "line": 152,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "Just do auto here.  No need to convert the type on the bind_front call (which produces an implementation defined object, so auto is acceptable)."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/entity_manager/perform_scan.cpp",
                    "line": 152,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "If i do `auto` it won't compile here. So i will write down the type here to make it compile. You can try it for yourself. I'm not posting the error here since it's super verbose and incomprehensible."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/entity_manager/perform_scan.cpp",
                    "line": 153,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "Capturing by \"this\" isn't safe in this instance.  Old code captured &io, which is also unsafe, but can be reasonably assumed to outlive the boost asio connection (and therefore any callback).  PerformScan have no lifetime promises at this level.  This is where we generally do the weak_from_this() trick to handle if the object has been destroyed before the callback is complete"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/entity_manager/perform_scan.cpp",
                    "line": 153,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "Made these functions static and declared outside of the class which resolve the issue with passing `this`."
                },
